{
  "id": "lakeshore_janis_ccs",
  "manufacturer": "Lake Shore Cryotronics (Environment by Janis)",
  "model": "CCS-series closed-cycle sample-in-vacuum cryostats (CCS-100, CCS-300S, CCS-400, CCS-400H)",
  "family": "cryogen-free closed-cycle-refrigerator optical cryostat, sample in vacuum, bottom-loading",
  "description": "Cryogen-free sample-in-vacuum optical cryostats. CCS-100 (<4 K to 325 K, optical), CCS-300S (<4 K to 325 K, subcompact optical), CCS-400 (<4 K to 500 K, optical high-temperature) and CCS-400H (<4 K to 800 K). The minimum temperature and cooling power depend on the cold head ordered (101: 0.2 W at 4.2 K; 408: 1 W at 4.2 K; 415: 1.5 W at 4.2 K; 418: 2 W at 4.2 K; 204N: 3 W at 10 K; 204: 7 W at 20 K, all bare-head ratings). Every cryostat ships with a Lake Shore temperature controller and calibrated sensor. CCS-300ST (non-optical) is documented but not profiled here.",
