  "notes": "CHECK REQUIRED: the CCS datasheet specification table (ccr-vacuum.pdf page 2) was read from pdftotext -layout output whose column alignment is imperfect. The cooldown-time values (ev_ls_0062 to ev_ls_0065), the per-cold-head minimum-temperature rows, and the CCS-400H '<5 K' lower bound are therefore marked inferred_estimate and must be verified against the rendered PDF before Lean accepts on them. The 4 K cold head choice (408 assumed) has no documented default; with the 101 head the cooling power is only 0.2 W at 4.2 K (ev_ls_0058), with 415/418 it is 1.5 W / 2 W (ev_ls_0056, ev_ls_0057). The 10 K-class heads (204, 204N) would raise the minimum temperature above 4 K. optical.clear_aperture 1.63 in (41402 um) comes from the generic Lake Shore window guide, which does not name the CCS models explicitly. Evidence file: data/evidence/lakeshore.json.",
